      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-251197",
      ":question/problem": "Consider a normally distributed population with unknown mean and variance, for which it is known that $95%$ of the observations lie between $-5.2$ and $4.8$, and this data is distributed symmetrically about the mean.\nUsing the empirical rule to estimate the population standard deviation, find the smallest sample size $n$ required to ensure that the margin of error for the $90%$ confidence interval for the population mean is at most $0.15$.\n\n*Hint: Use the fact that $P(Z > 1.645) = 0.05$, where $Z\u223cN(0, 1)$.*\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
